WEBVTT

00:04:26.397 --> 00:04:30.297
And whenever anyone
tells me a ghost story,

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.697
I ask them two questions.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.097
First:

00:04:34.097 --> 00:04:36.163
"What do you think this ghost wanted?"

00:04:36.497 --> 00:04:39.163
And second, because most people
are ambivalent

00:04:39.197 --> 00:04:42.130
about whether or not
the ghost actually exists,

00:04:42.163 --> 00:04:45.797
I ask, "What is it that you want
from the ghost?"

00:04:46.863 --> 00:04:50.097
The first question
is pretty easy to answer.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:53.763
I have found that most ghosts
fall into one of three categories,

00:04:53.797 --> 00:04:56.663
and what they all want
is pretty much the same --

00:04:56.697 --> 00:04:58.263
to be acknowledged.

00:04:58.863 --> 00:05:02.030
The first type of ghost
is the kind I started studying.